    "it is what the plan writer reads first. Kinds: hook, class, function, constant, meta,",
    "table, js. dynamic:true marks a hook built at runtime (cannot be verified by grep).",
    "source.type: wporg (zip available) | changelog (version only) | core | php.",
    "source.installed: the slug on the box's stage site -- WordPress's own updater reports a new version for anything installed there, licence or not, so that is the primary signal for paid plugins; changelog pages are the fallback when nothing is installed."
